-- @@ L5-21 verbatim
/-!
# Direct sums and graded products of families of dg modules

For a family `M : ι → Type*` of dg `A`-modules:

* the direct sum `⨁ i, M i` is a dg `A`-module, graded by `(⨁ i, M i)ⁿ = {x | ∀ i, x i ∈ (M i)ⁿ}`
  (the finitely supported families of homogeneous elements of degree `n`), with componentwise
  differential; the inclusions `DG.DGModuleHom.lof A M i : M i →ᵈᵍ[A] ⨁ i, M i` and the map
  `DG.DGModuleHom.toModule` out of the direct sum are morphisms. This is the coproduct in the
  category of dg modules.
* the graded product `DG.GradedPi A M`: the product `∀ i, M i` is not graded by the products of
  the homogeneous components (a family of homogeneous elements of unbounded degrees is not a
  finite sum of homogeneous families), so the product in the category of dg modules is the
  submodule of `∀ i, M i` generated by the homogeneous families, `⨁ₙ ∏ᵢ (M i)ⁿ`. Its graded
  pieces are the homogeneous families of degree `n`, the projections `DG.DGModuleHom.proj` and the
  pairing `DG.DGModuleHom.pi` are morphisms. This is the product in the category of dg modules.
-/


